      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4fa2001f-8608-56be-a159-d4678ca16da0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Archduke John of Austria, Eugène de Beauharnais\n- Events: Battle of Sacile, Battle of Fontana Fredda, Clash at Pordenone, Revolutions of 1848\n- Organizations: House of Habsburg-Lorraine, German Empire\n- Roles: Austrian field marshal, Imperial regent\n\nFacts:\n- Archduke John of Austria was born on 20 January 1782 and was a member of the House of Habsburg-Lorraine.\n- On 15 April 1809, the Clash at Pordenone took place as the companion action to the Battle of Sacile.\n- On 16 April 1809, the Battle of Sacile, also known as the Battle of Fontana Fredda, ended with Archduke John of Austria's Austrian army defeating Eugène de Beauharnais's Franco-Italian army and forcing it to retreat.\n- During the Revolutions of 1848, Archduke John of Austria served as Imperial regent of the short-lived German Empire.\n- Archduke John of Austria was an Austrian field marshal.\n- Archduke John of Austria died on 11 May 1859.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7cc708b2-4c47-5dfe-9da1-bc3ffa1418a6",
        "text": "Page: Battle of Sacile. Sentence: The Battle of Sacile (also known as the Battle of Fontana Fredda) on 16 April 1809 and its companion Clash at Pordenone on 15 April saw an Austrian army commanded by Archduke John of Austria defeat a Franco-Italian army led by Eugène de Beauharnais and force it to retreat.\nPage: Archduke John of Austria. Sentence: Archduke John of Austria (German: \"Erzherzog Johann Baptist Joseph Fabian Sebastian von Österreich\" ; 20 January 1782 – 11 May 1859), a member of the House of Habsburg-Lorraine, was an Austrian field marshal and Imperial regent (\"Reichsverweser\") of the short-lived German Empire during the Revolutions of 1848.",
